WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:02.623
- Elder sister, younger sister.

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.750
Number one and number two.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:05.750
- Who is number one?

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:08.940
- You.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:09.773
Course.

00:00:11.179 --> 00:00:13.179
(drums)

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.630
- Hello and welcome to beneath the crown.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:18.890
I'm Laura Jackson and you
are in the right place

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:21.210
if you want to delve deeper
into the true stories

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.420
that inspired season three of our show.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.810
Lets roll back the years
to join Princess Margaret

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:29.098
on her memorable tour of the
United States of America.

00:00:29.098 --> 00:00:29.931
(video reel)

00:00:29.931 --> 00:00:31.890
(jazz music)

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.820
- It's 1965 and while the
world is being conquered

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.620
by four lads called The Beatles,

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.570
Princess Margaret and Lord
Snowdon are too busy partying

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.490
to do much in the way of royal duties.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:42.323
- Quite right.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.820
- [Laura] So as a public show of unity

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.940
they embarked on an intent three week tour

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.353
of the United States.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:53.630
Being an informal visit,

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:55.250
the 12 members of the royal party

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.250
had to take commercial flights.

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:00.070
(airplane engine whooshing)

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:03.540
Margaret became only the
second senior royal to do so.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:06.549
(classical jazz music)

00:01:06.549 --> 00:01:08.700
(camera shutter)

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.280
Margaret visiting for the first time

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.528
was greeted very warmly indeed.

00:01:12.528 --> 00:01:13.700
(crowd cheers)

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:17.780
Still there was an outcry over
the entire 64,000 pound cost

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:18.770
of the tour,

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:21.839
roughly 1.2 million in today's money.

00:01:21.839 --> 00:01:24.256
(jazz music)

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.520
The first few days of
the tour in San Francisco

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.850
saw Margaret and Tony on a
whirlwind of social engagements

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:34.453
and sightseeing, often
drawing large crowds.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.410
They attended a fashion show

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.420
to promote British clothing.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:44.260
It's not often you see models
curtsying on the catwalk.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.520
Fashion was very close
to Margaret's heart.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.640
She traveled to America with 79 suitcases

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.133
of British made garments.

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:55.890
The couple was soon
mingling with the stars

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:57.313
at Universal studios.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.430
Joining actors Paul
Newman and Julie Andrews

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:05.063
on set with legendary
director Alfred Hitchcock.

00:02:06.016 --> 00:02:07.950
(jazz music)

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:10.700
(camera shutter)

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:15.700
A, "Welcome to Hollywood"
bash was thrown for them,

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:17.400
including guests such as Bob Hope,

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:19.323
Frank Sinatra,

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.820
Elizabeth Taylor and Richard Burton.

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:24.810
Legendary "Wizard of Oz" star Judy Garland

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.370
was also in attendance.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.931
And Margaret couldn't
resist asking for a song.

00:02:28.931 --> 00:02:30.190
- Music.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.530
- Royal protocol requires
no one to leave a party

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:34.410
before any royal in attendance.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.920
Not ideal when you're a film
star with an early start

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.300
and your royal guest is a party animal.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.850
Frank Sinatra and Mia
Farrow managed to sneak out

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.400
discreetly through the kitchen.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.660
But they were reportedly granted approval

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:48.380
from Margaret before hand.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:50.840
The late nights soon took
their toll on Margaret

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:53.446
who lost her voice with laryngitis.

00:02:53.446 --> 00:02:54.780
(airplane whooshing)

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:57.420
The next leg of the tour saw
an unwell Margaret and Tony

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:00.293
head to Arizona for a
little rest and relaxation.

00:03:00.293 --> 00:03:01.560
(coughs)

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.950
The experience was very
unusual for the royals

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:07.128
and provided some rather
peculiar photo opportunities.

00:03:07.128 --> 00:03:09.545
(jazz music)

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.993
But at least Tony got to play a cowboy.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:17.140
More late nights led to a
series of canceled engagements

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:20.022
blamed by the press on royal hangovers.

00:03:20.022 --> 00:03:22.820
- (exhales) I look hideous.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:24.640
- You look a bit tired,

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.890
it's only to be expected after your

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:29.700
heroics.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.941
And now you must sleep.

00:03:31.941 --> 00:03:32.774
(kiss sound)

00:03:32.774 --> 00:03:34.220
- With the tour at the halfway mark,

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:36.420
off the exhausted couple
flew to Washington.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:40.890
A tour of various landmarks followed,

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:42.603
including the Lincoln Memorial.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.030
But the tour took a turn for the worse,

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.050
as a New York Times publish a story

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:50.400
accusing the royal party

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.753
of leaving a trail of unpaid
bills behind in Arizona.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:57.400
The British embassy reportedly
stepped in to settle up

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.193
and avoid further embarrassment.

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:02.590
Attention turned to the White House dinner

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:04.110
with President Johnson.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.310
- Your royal highness.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:06.514
- President Johnson.

00:04:06.514 --> 00:04:08.931
(jazz music)

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.507
- The event went down a treat

00:04:13.507 --> 00:04:14.340
(camera shutter)

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:17.219
as the couples hit it off and
danced long into the night.

00:04:17.219 --> 00:04:18.539
(jazz music)

00:04:18.539 --> 00:04:22.840
(people laughing and chatting)

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:25.760
And so the couple moved on
to the final leg of the tour

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.154
in New York.

00:04:27.154 --> 00:04:28.890
(jazz music)

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:31.330
The adoring crowds were still out in force

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.810
with 1,500 fans turning
up to see the Snowdon's

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:35.423
visit the Empire State Building.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:39.500
New york engagements included a visit

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.060
to the United Nations headquarters,

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:44.103
a trip to The Museum of Modern Art,

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:46.240
and an evening charity ball

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.253
for the Winston Churchill Memorial Fund.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.270
The royal family,

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.300
the ultimate dance floor filler.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.180
With the tour drawing to a close

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:58.050
a farewell supper and dance
was held for Margaret and Tony

00:04:58.050 --> 00:04:59.810
on Tuesday the 23rd of November,

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:03.240
at the prestigious Four Seasons
Restaurant, in Manhattan.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:05.870
Margaret was still
going strong at 3:00 a.m

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:08.180
when she ordered a full cooked breakfast.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:10.350
Spare a thought for those
who were unable to leave,

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:11.850
because of the royal protocol.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:15.710
And so after 21 days of late nights

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.580
the royal party departed.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:20.340
Margaret had won lesion of
new admirers in the U.S,

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.220
and the couple have
patriotically championed

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:25.280
British industry and
interest while in town.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:27.430
The fashion critics were
less than impressed.

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.480
In an article widely circulated,

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.520
Women's Wear Daily called Margaret's style

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:35.152
a schizophrenic mixture of chic
and sheer fashion disaster.

00:05:35.152 --> 00:05:36.620
Ouch.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:39.460
The royal party boarded
another commercial flight

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:43.120
and were hit with a excess
baggage fee of 5,000 pounds,

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:45.960
that's over 95,000
pounds in today's money.

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:47.304
- It is my burden.

00:05:47.304 --> 00:05:48.362
(jazz music)

00:05:48.362 --> 00:05:49.690
(airplane whooshes)

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:51.650
- Extravagant expenditure aside,

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:55.370
the couple returned as
darlings of the United States.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:57.060
But while bridges were built abroad,

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.700
the cracks continue to widen

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.400
between Margaret and Tony at home.

00:06:02.141 --> 00:06:06.058
(jazz music dramatically ends)

